# GIBSON-REPLICATION BAND: easy (route 10-25 m; Gibson easy is geodesic 1.5-3 m).
#
# Layered on the CHECKPOINT'S OWN training overlay (BENCH_BASE_OVERLAY, default
# v30's), so the env, reward and network match what the policy trained on and
# only the episode distribution changes.
#
# BINS AT CARLA SCALE (user 2026-11-01, "use longer distance in carla"): 10-25 /
# 25-50 / 50-100 m. The policy trained on goals up to 25 m, so medium and hard
# need the map built from the exploration trace -- the comparison the peer's
# Gibson map arms make.
#
# WHY EACH DIFFICULTY HAS ITS OWN BAND. Probing showed the standard 5-25 m draw
# lands almost all goals at ~20-25 m (85% of origins sit before a junction and
# GOAL_PAST_JUNCTION keeps only distances >= 15 m past it), so bins cannot be
# filled by filtering one draw; each is GENERATED from its own band, as
# Mezghani's set was generated per difficulty. The band is part of the episode
# (a seed replayed under another band is a different episode), and it must be
# set HERE: train_sac.sbatch hard-exports GOAL_DIST_MIN/MAX before sourcing
# the overlay, so a band given on the command line is silently overwritten.
#
# Draws 10..24 m (step 1): route distance >= the drawn lane distance, so drawing
# up to 25 would put the top draws in the medium bin and waste them.
. "$REPO/${BENCH_BASE_OVERLAY:-slurm/v30_overlay.env}"
export BENCH_BAND=easy GOAL_DIST_MIN=10 GOAL_DIST_MAX=24 GOAL_DIST_STEP=1
# Gibson's success radius. 2 m is scored from the same run (EpisodeTracker).
export GOAL_RADIUS_M=1.0
